<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prithviraj Chauhan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1166–1192</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Prithviraja III</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prithviraja III, known as Prithviraj <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhan</a>, was a king of the Chahamana dynasty of Shakambhari, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a>. He fought the Chandelas and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a> at the first Battle of Tarain in 1191, but was defeated and killed after the second battle in 1192, opening northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> to Ghurid conquest. He became a hero of later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> legend.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prithviraj-chauhan.jpg" alt="Prithviraj Chauhan" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Posthumous_painting_depicting_Prithviraj_Chauhan_from_Kota_(colour).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
